-- why a meaning stops without being undefined: the loop fuel ran out; the Target does not offer
-- what was asked (a 128-bit integer on i386, a pointer↔integer conversion under pi-refused); an
-- operation was applied at a kind it has no meaning at (a reader's error, not the program's:
-- adding pointers, a value whose constructor is not the kind's); the standard leaves the result
-- unspecified and no parameter here fixes it (an order between pointers into different allocations)
data Stop = st-fuel | st-unsupported | st-ill-typed | st-unspecified
